From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:41:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Improve with AI redesigns the site in rounds,
 checked and undoable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Improve asked once for CSS from an outline and applied whatever came
back. Now it works like a designer with a review:

- The AI gets the page measured: viewport and light/dark, landmarks and
  big regions, repeated components, the type scale in use, background,
  text and accent colours, the site's theme variables, density, shapes,
  and the outline; plus a screenshot (JPEG, at most 1280 px wide) for the
  AIs that see pictures: Claude on the key (an image block) and Claude
  Code (one stream-json user message on stdin, still with no tools).
- A senior product designer's brief: one palette with AA contrast, a
  type scale, a 4 px rhythm, radius and shadows, readable line lengths,
  hover/active/focus-visible states, dense apps kept dense, the theme
  respected; only CSS, nothing hidden, layout and controls intact.
- Up to three rounds within about 90 s: the CSS is applied, the page is
  photographed again and the AI reviews it ("Reviewing… 2/3",
  "Polishing… 3/3" in the editor's button) until it says it's done; a
  round that fails or runs late keeps the last good CSS.
- Every round's CSS is checked before it reaches the page
  (boost_improve.cc): parsed, at most 96 KB; whatever hides content or
  controls (display: none, visibility, opacity near 0, zero sizes,
  clipping, masks, off-screen offsets, pointer-events: none, transparent
  text), loads from the internet (url() other than data:, @import other
  than Google Fonts), runs code or animates is taken out, every
  declaration gets !important. What was taken out goes to the next round.
- Clutter (ads, cookie banners) comes as a separate "hide" list, only
  when asked for; checked by selector and on the page, and saved as zaps,
  each with its own Undo in Zap.
- While it works the page shows it (boost_magic.ts, drawn by the browser
  over the tab, so never in the AI's screenshots, and never taking the
  pointer): an iridescent glow sweeping round the page's edges, a faint
  shimmer, a status pill with the round ("Designing… 1/3 · going for
  “warm editorial”", "Reviewing… 2/3 · fixing what the checks took
  out"), a soft veil lifting off each round's new look, then "Done" with
  Undo for a moment. The Improve button flows in the same colours. Only
  transform and opacity animate; with reduced motion it all stands still.
- The direction field steers it ("like Linear", "warm editorial");
  empty is a redesign of the AI's own. The result is the boost's CSS (in
  Code, to edit); Undo puts the boost back as it was.

